  <h3>1. What CabinetDrafter does</h3>
  <p>CabinetDrafter is a single-file local browser tool for designing cabinet runs using frameless or face-frame construction. It calculates drawer boxes, doors, open cubbies, shelf openings, plywood parts and sheet nesting, and renders the cabinet lineup directly in the page. SketchUp export is optional. It does not need a web server or an online account.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Build a lineup of drawer/mixed cabinets, single-door cabinets, and open-shelf cabinets.</li>
    <li>Enter drawer box heights and open-space heights from bottom to top.</li>
    <li>Use inches or millimeters without changing the underlying geometry.</li>
    <li>Generate a plywood BOM, detailed cut-list CSV, and 4 × 8 sheet-planning diagrams.</li>
    <li>Orbit and inspect the cabinet model directly in the browser and save the current view as PNG.</li>
    <li>Optionally generate a Ruby script that builds and saves the model in SketchUp Pro.</li>
    <li>Save the project to JSON and keep a browser-local recovery copy automatically.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>2. First-time workflow</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Choose units.</strong> Inches and millimeters are only display/entry choices; CabinetDrafter keeps canonical geometry in inches internally for SketchUp compatibility.</li>
    <li><strong>Edit the Cabinets table.</strong> Set a label, type, width, quantity, vertical stack/opening heights, and shelf count where appropriate.</li>
    <li><strong>Review the sizing preview.</strong> Fix anything shown as a warning before relying on the cut list.</li>
    <li><strong>Review the BOM and sheet layouts.</strong> Grain-sensitive cherry parts are kept oriented when Preserve cherry grain direction is enabled.</li>
    <li><strong>Click Save Project JSON.</strong> Pick a normal file such as <code>my_kitchen.json</code>. Supported browsers will then auto-save that same file as you edit.</li>
    <li><strong>Click Download Ruby script.</strong> CabinetDrafter shows the exact <code>load ...</code> command to paste into SketchUp.</li>
    <li><strong>In SketchUp Pro:</strong> open <em>Window → Ruby Console</em>, paste the command, and press Enter. Regenerating replaces the prior <em>Generated Cabinet Lineup</em> group.</li>
  </ol>

  <h3>3. Cabinet types</h3>
  <table class="help-table">
